{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467447-a-sunny-day-in-venice","id":1467447,"title":"A sunny day in Venice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-11T08:05:19-08:00","id":1467447,"title":"A sunny day in Venice","content":"Venice is sinking. This is not news, or at least not new news, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9mjyJ8ANt0o\" data-code=\"9mjyJ8ANt0o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9mjyJ8ANt0o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Seeing people wander about is thigh-high waders and it all becoming &quot;normal&quot; is interesting. But I am posting this here to encourage discussion about how this will impact the Giovanni (and other Venice dwelling vampires). Drowning will not kill them, but flooding will ruin the antique furniture in a low-set haven. And not all vampires are alright with sleeping underwater in any case.<br /> <br /> Edit to Add: Sloshing around in shin deep water should also make it harder to sneak around, look majestic, and so on. And you better hope none of your ingredients for thaumatury need to stay dry, unless you start keeping them in ziplock bags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 11-11-2021, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T22:16:46-08:00","id":1467526,"title":"","content":"Outside those Giovanni that actually live in the waters of the city, that's a big question. I think most Giovanni are probably investing in finding solutions for the problem, as for them this isn't nearly as abstract as it is for mortals (and it isn't that much). No matter how much time it takes for the city to become a drowned ruin, they'll live to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T23:26:52-08:00","id":1467528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467447-a-sunny-day-in-venice#post1467447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Venice is sinking. This is not news, or at least not new news, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9mjyJ8ANt0o\" data-code=\"9mjyJ8ANt0o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9mjyJ8ANt0o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Seeing people wander about is thigh-high waders and it all becoming &quot;normal&quot; is interesting. But I am posting this here to encourage discussion about how this will impact the Giovanni (and other Venice dwelling vampires). Drowning will not kill them, but flooding will ruin the antique furniture in a low-set haven. And not all vampires are alright with sleeping underwater in any case.<br /> <br /> Edit to Add: Sloshing around in shin deep water should also make it harder to sneak around, look majestic, and so on. And you better hope none of your ingredients for thaumatury need to stay dry, unless you start keeping them in ziplock bags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm. We venetians always lived like this. During the 80's we had the worst high water rising. Almost every year we get some damages but its basically normal and we are ready for it. I don't live in venice anymore but that's just normal. It always has been. We use apposite wood and iron barricade and we use to work and go to school with appropriate equipment. <br /> A true disaster is very rare. Vampires just have to organize their heavens on some kind of blinded last floors or on the mainland. Venice has a huge sub urban zone outside the island. Also, venice has a weird architecture. Some zones do not or barely suffer the high water. During the last 15 years the goverment builded the Mose project , some kind of underwater dam that partially solve the problem, sometimes. The project funders were of course all corrupted and stole money. Not a surprise. Which is a 100% Giovanni thing.<br /> <br /> At the table we almost Never followed what the book said about the giovanni organization , like the skycraper , the mafia vibe but the actual main place in venice and other things .... many things are just, lets say, funny ..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 11-12-2021, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T18:17:39-08:00","id":1467621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467447-a-sunny-day-in-venice?p=1467528#post1467528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehm. We venetians always lived like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is the &quot;always&quot; of a person and the &quot;always&quot; of an undead. Climate change is increasing the frequency of Risings every year, and the population is shrinking.<br /> <br /> None of this is enough to change things drastically in 20, 30 years. But the Giovanni remember the city centuries ago. Some still remember its apex in the late 15th century. Their long term thought isn't 30 years, it's at least 300.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, they may actually be behind the trends and preparing to live in an underwater complex with the city above increasingly becoming a resort for tourists more than an actual city, and that does seems to make sense with what I saw residents talking about the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}